# Dialogue and narration
@scenario tutorial_lesson_20
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code shy]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/20_dialogue_presentation.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt mode]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: JVN supports standard dialogue and NVL presentation. The next two lines use NVL so you can compare a page of text with a single dialogue box.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
# region mode
[mode dialogue nvl]
narrator: {i}NVL, paragraph one.{/i} Advance once and watch where the following paragraph appears.
narrator: {i}NVL, paragraph two.{/i} Check how much of the previous text remains visible.
[mode dialogue standard]
# endregion
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
ginger: The script has switched back to {b}standard{/b}. This line uses the regular dialogue box and speaker name again.
ginger: Find [mode dialogue nvl] and [mode dialogue standard]. Add another short paragraph between them and replay the sequence.
ginger: Move the same paragraph below the second command. Its text stays the same, but it now uses the standard layout.
ginger: A dialogue mode affects subsequent lines. Locate the instruction that switches to NVL, read the paragraphs it encloses, then locate the switch back to standard.
ginger: Use identical wording in both modes when testing layout. This makes it easier to separate presentation behaviour from differences in the amount of text.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Trace a mode boundary -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: Why restore the dialogue mode at the boundary?
> So the character art is deleted. -> retry
> So the next scene opens with its intended layout. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The mode controls text presentation. Consider which layout the first line of the next section should use.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Set the intended mode explicitly so the following section opens in the correct layout.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_20]
[flag tutorial_done_20]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_4]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/20_dialogue_presentation.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt mode]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Add a short third paragraph just before the switch back to standard. Advance through all three paragraphs and note how much of the sequence remains on screen.
ginger: Move that same paragraph below the switch to standard. Its speaker and content are unchanged. Compare the surrounding UI, speaker label and earlier visible text.
ginger: Follow each route that can leave an NVL section. If one branch jumps over the reset, the next line can inherit a mode you never intended for that branch.
ginger: When a later scene looks wrong, find the last executed mode command on that particular route. Its location in the file alone does not tell you whether the player reached it.
@label practice_question
ginger: One branch jumps past the switch back to standard. Which state should you inspect on the following line?
> The locale table. -> practice_hint
> The active dialogue presentation mode. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The same text can display in either layout. Trace the last mode instruction actually reached on that branch.
[jump practice_question]
@label practice_result
ginger: The branch skipped the command that restored the layout. Put the common reset where every outgoing route reaches it and retest both branches.
ginger: Compare this exact sentence in both modes. Advance after each copy.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[mode dialogue nvl]
narrator: The last line is visible.
[mode dialogue standard]
narrator: The last line is visible.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the exercise again -> practice
> Back to topics -> return_hub
